WEBVTT

00:07:58.688 --> 00:08:02.807
Who knows how to structure spaces
for the public good?

00:08:04.053 --> 00:08:05.803
And it turns out, this is a question

00:08:05.827 --> 00:08:08.788
people have been thinking about
for a long time about cities.

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:12.450
Cities were the original platforms.

00:08:12.474 --> 00:08:13.960
Two-sided marketplace?

00:08:13.984 --> 00:08:15.276
Check.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.509
Place to keep up with old friends
and distant relatives?

00:08:18.533 --> 00:08:19.699
Check.

00:08:19.723 --> 00:08:21.660
Vector for viral sharing?

00:08:21.684 --> 00:08:23.049
Check.

00:08:23.073 --> 00:08:25.247
In fact, cities have encountered

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:28.910
a lot of the same social
and political challenges

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:31.021
that platforms are now encountering.